WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.090 position:50% size:92% align:center
For category zero, the selected input token IDs

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.317 position:50% size:92% align:center
are zero, two, five and seven.

00:00:06.537 --> 00:00:09.545 position:50% size:92% align:center
Their threads need unique output positions even

00:00:09.545 --> 00:00:11.273 position:50% size:92% align:center
if the GPU does not execute

00:00:11.273 --> 00:00:13.129 position:50% size:92% align:center
those threads in input order.

00:00:15.149 --> 00:00:18.300 position:50% size:92% align:center
The flag kernel writes selection flags. The scan

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.385 position:50% size:92% align:center
kernel uses completed flags to produce offsets,

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:23.683 position:50% size:92% align:center
and scatter uses completed offsets.

00:00:23.903 --> 00:00:26.719 position:50% size:92% align:center
The launches use one ordered stream. A block

00:00:26.719 --> 00:00:29.279 position:50% size:92% align:center
barrier is not the mechanism that orders

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.135 position:50% size:92% align:center
these separate kernel phases.

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:36.258 position:50% size:92% align:center
Token five has two earlier selected tokens, so

00:00:36.258 --> 00:00:38.147 position:50% size:92% align:center
its exclusive offset is two.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.190 position:50% size:92% align:center
Its scatter writes token ID five into output

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.757 position:50% size:92% align:center
position two. The address comes from the

00:00:43.757 --> 00:00:46.388 position:50% size:92% align:center
completed prefix, not from arrival order.

00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:51.237 position:50% size:92% align:center
Pause and predict the destination if token

00:00:51.237 --> 00:00:54.403 position:50% size:92% align:center
seven’s write is inspected before token zero’s.

00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:56.534 position:50% size:92% align:center
Does writing first give token

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.313 position:50% size:92% align:center
seven output position zero?

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.038 position:50% size:92% align:center
Token seven writes position three because three

00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:09.509 position:50% size:92% align:center
selected tokens precede it in the input.

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:13.000 position:50% size:92% align:center
The model inspects writes in reverse order and

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.129 position:50% size:92% align:center
still produces token IDs zero, two, five and

00:01:16.129 --> 00:01:18.263 position:50% size:92% align:center
seven in the completed output.

00:01:20.283 --> 00:01:23.475 position:50% size:92% align:center
Stream dependencies make flags and offsets ready

00:01:23.475 --> 00:01:26.401 position:50% size:92% align:center
before scatter. Prefix offsets determine the

00:01:26.401 --> 00:01:28.795 position:50% size:92% align:center
stable destination of each survivor.

00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:31.925 position:50% size:92% align:center
The SMs may execute independent writes in

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.191 position:50% size:92% align:center
different orders; the completed output’s order

00:01:35.191 --> 00:01:37.463 position:50% size:92% align:center
follows the address calculation.
